into office that does not

1235
01:13:08.616 --> 01:13:11.450
believe in the science
of climate change,

1236
01:13:11.486 --> 01:13:14.487
do they have the capacity
and the power to dismantle

1237
01:13:14.522 --> 01:13:16.021
everything that you've
already worked for?

1238
01:13:16.057 --> 01:13:19.458
Even if somebody came in,
campaigning on denying

1239
01:13:19.494 --> 01:13:24.964
climate science, reality has
a way of, you know,

1240
01:13:24.999 --> 01:13:27.900
hitting you in the nose if
you're not paying attention.

1241
01:13:27.935 --> 01:13:32.705
And I think that the public is
starting to realize the science,

1242
01:13:32.740 --> 01:13:35.841
in part because
it's indisputable.

1243
01:13:35.877 --> 01:13:38.644
I, I admire your optimism.

1244
01:13:38.679 --> 01:13:39.512
Yeah.
But

1245
01:13:39.547 --> 01:13:41.180
you start to look at
the science,

1246
01:13:41.215 --> 01:13:43.082
look at what's going on
in the Antarctic and,

1247
01:13:43.117 --> 01:13:46.018
and scientists saying that
there are sections of ice that

1248
01:13:46.053 --> 01:13:49.688
guarantee four to six
meters of ocean level rise,

1249
01:13:49.724 --> 01:13:52.958
which will be catastrophic
for the future.

1250
01:13:52.994 --> 01:13:56.028
You are the leader
of the Free World.

1251
01:13:56.063 --> 01:13:59.565
You have access to information
that most people do not.

1252
01:13:59.600 --> 01:14:03.903
What makes you terrified
for the future?

1253
01:14:03.938 --> 01:14:07.540
Uh, a huge portion
of the world's population

1254
01:14:07.575 --> 01:14:09.708
lives near oceans.
Mhm.

1255
01:14:09.744 --> 01:14:16.448
If they start moving,
then you start seeing,

1256
01:14:16.484 --> 01:14:18.951
um, scarce resources.

1257
01:14:18.986 --> 01:14:21.854
The subject of competition
between populations.

1258
01:14:21.889 --> 01:14:24.423
This is the reason why
the Pentagon has said,

1259
01:14:24.458 --> 01:14:26.058
this is a national
security issue.

1260
01:14:26.093 --> 01:14:27.993
This isn't just an
environmental issue.

1261
01:14:28.029 --> 01:14:30.496
This is a national
security issue.

1262
01:14:30.531 --> 01:14:36.168
You know, in addition to just
the sadness that I would feel if

1263
01:14:36.203 --> 01:14:40.573
my kids can never see a glacier,
the way I saw when I went up

1264
01:14:40.608 --> 01:14:43.709
to Alaska, uh, you know,
that's the romantic side of it.

1265
01:14:43.744 --> 01:14:46.579
That's the side that takes
a walk with my daughters

1266
01:14:46.614 --> 01:14:49.148
and I wanna be able to, them
to see, or my grandkids,

1267
01:14:49.183 --> 01:14:50.816
I want them to see the
same things as I saw

1268
01:14:50.851 --> 01:14:51.984
as I was growing up.

1269
01:14:52.019 --> 01:14:55.788
Even if you were
unsentimental about that,

1270
01:14:55.823 --> 01:14:58.891
in very hard-headed terms,
you've gotta worry about

1271
01:14:58.926 --> 01:15:00.759
the national security
implications of this,

1272
01:15:00.795 --> 01:15:04.930
and the capacity for the
existing world order

1273
01:15:04.966 --> 01:15:07.866
as we understand it to
survive the kinds of strains

1274
01:15:07.902 --> 01:15:10.102
that the scientists are
predicting without action.

1275
01:15:10.137 --> 01:15:14.106
This is why we have
to take action now.

1276
01:15:14.141 --> 01:15:17.476
If we keep pushing keep prodding
and most importantly keep

1277
01:15:17.511 --> 01:15:21.113
educating the public
there's no reason why, uh,

1278
01:15:21.148 --> 01:15:23.983
we can't solve this
problem in time.

1279
01:15:24.018 --> 01:15:25.150
Thank you for your time, Mr. President.

1280
01:15:25.186 --> 01:15:26.118
You bet.

1281
01:15:26.153 --> 01:15:27.386
Thanks for the good
work you're doing.

1282
01:15:27.421 --> 01:15:28.721
Thank you so much.
Alright. Good?

1283
01:15:37.798 --> 01:15:41.467
I have realized that as
a science community we have not

1284
01:15:41.502 --> 01:15:46.705
done the best job, frankly,
of communicating this threat

1285
01:15:46.741 --> 01:15:50.309
to the public.

1286
01:15:50.344 --> 01:15:53.345
But when you go up there and
see it with your own eye,

1287
01:15:53.381 --> 01:15:58.350
how thin the world's
atmosphere is,

1288
01:15:58.386 --> 01:16:02.488
tiny little onion
skin around the earth.

1289
01:16:02.523 --> 01:16:05.391
That's all the oxygen that
we breathe, that's the CO2,

1290
01:16:05.426 --> 01:16:08.160
everything we burn goes into it.

1291
01:16:08.195 --> 01:16:11.497
It's an astonishingly
fragile film.

1292
01:16:15.136 --> 01:16:17.603
You know, I knew intellectually
how the earth's system works,

1293
01:16:17.638 --> 01:16:19.471
'cause that's what I've
been doing for 20 years.

1294
01:16:19.507 --> 01:16:21.607
To see how the
atmosphere and the ocean,

1295
01:16:21.642 --> 01:16:24.176
all the elements in the
system work together.

1296
01:16:24.211 --> 01:16:25.511
So I understood it
intellectually.

1297
01:16:25.546 --> 01:16:27.379
Mhm.

1298
01:16:27.415 --> 01:16:30.082
But it's like being
an ant trying to understand

1299
01:16:30.117 --> 01:16:32.651
what an elephant looks like by
crawling all over the elephant.

1300
01:16:36.390 --> 01:16:37.523
But when you're
up there in orbit,

1301
01:16:37.558 --> 01:16:41.694
and you can see 1200 miles
in any direction, I mean,

1302
01:16:41.729 --> 01:16:42.728
let me tell you.

1303
01:16:42.763 --> 01:16:45.597
It's kind of a revelation.

1304
01:16:45.633 --> 01:16:48.734
Seeing all the cities at night,
millions of people all working

1305
01:16:48.769 --> 01:16:51.236
away, doing something.

1306
01:16:51.272 --> 01:16:52.504
Come around the day
side of the world,

1307
01:16:52.540 --> 01:16:54.173
seeing the natural systems.

1308
01:16:54.208 --> 01:16:57.676
The hurricanes, huge,
great big wheels, you know,

1309
01:16:57.712 --> 01:17:00.112
over the oceans.

1310
01:17:00.147 --> 01:17:03.182
Saw the Amazon River
go between my feet.

1311
01:17:03.217 --> 01:17:05.484
For like five minutes, you know,
I have a whole green carpet

1312
01:17:05.519 --> 01:17:06.552
either side.

1313
01:17:06.587 --> 01:17:09.388
Just beautiful, all
the way out to the sea.

1314
01:17:09.423 --> 01:17:11.323
And you know there was the sun
coming up over the Amazon,

1315
01:17:11.358 --> 01:17:14.626
the whole forest waking up, and
doing what it does every day,

1316
01:17:14.662 --> 01:17:17.029
you know. Breathing
in and breathing out.

1317
01:17:17.064 --> 01:17:20.632
So I, I, you know, at the end
of all that I became immensely

1318
01:17:20.668 --> 01:17:23.635
fond, more fond of
the planet. You know?

1319
01:17:23.671 --> 01:17:25.137
Which I never thought about
when I actually just live

1320
01:17:25.172 --> 01:17:26.238
on the surface.

1321
01:17:26.273 --> 01:17:28.707
I'm also kind of fond of
the people on there, too.

1322
01:17:28.743 --> 01:17:31.777
It's like being taken away from
your family and coming back.

1323
01:17:31.812 --> 01:17:37.182
And um, you know,
I wish it all well.

1324
01:17:37.218 --> 01:17:40.519
I, uh, just before Christmas
I got told I got pancreatic

1325
01:17:40.554 --> 01:17:42.387
cancer.

1326
01:17:42.423 --> 01:17:46.425
Stage 4, so it's also elsewhere
in me, not just in one place.

1327
01:17:46.460 --> 01:17:48.761
So um, you know, the, the odds
are I won't be around

1328
01:17:48.796 --> 01:17:50.562
for very long.

1329
01:17:50.598 --> 01:17:54.166
You know, it's a very
small chance of survival.

1330
01:17:54.201 --> 01:17:58.137
So, uh, that's really
motivated me to think about

1331
01:17:58.172 --> 01:18:01.540
what's important to do, and what
can I contribute in the time

1332
01:18:01.575 --> 01:18:04.176
I have left.

1333
01:18:04.211 --> 01:18:09.248
So this is a model
simulation of the earth, now,

1334
01:18:09.283 --> 01:18:11.650
we have about 20 satellites
that are dedicated to looking

1335
01:18:11.685 --> 01:18:14.319
at the earth, every day.

1336
01:18:14.355 --> 01:18:16.789
One looks at clouds, one looks
at the sea surface temperature,

1337
01:18:16.824 --> 01:18:19.491
Oko looks at carbon dioxide
in the atmosphere.

1338
01:18:19.527 --> 01:18:22.795
All this information comes in,
and this is the tool we use

1339
01:18:22.830 --> 01:18:24.663
to do climate simulation.

1340
01:18:24.698 --> 01:18:27.633
Here's an example of one thing
we could see: this is

1341
01:18:27.668 --> 01:18:31.036
ocean surface temperature,
as measured from space.

1342
01:18:31.071 --> 01:18:33.572
This is the whole world's
surface temperature.

1343
01:18:33.607 --> 01:18:37.276
You can see the
poles melting, there.

1344
01:18:37.311 --> 01:18:38.243
Wow.

1345
01:18:38.279 --> 01:18:39.178
Yeah.
It's amazing.

1346
01:18:39.213 --> 01:18:40.245
This is the
way to do it man.

1347
01:18:40.281 --> 01:18:42.481
This is the way to really
see what's going on.

1348
01:18:42.516 --> 01:18:43.682
Here's the Gulf
Stream, look at this.

1349
01:18:43.717 --> 01:18:46.451
It's like a motion of the ocean.

1350
01:18:46.487 --> 01:18:48.420
This is like
a great piece of art.

1351
01:18:48.455 --> 01:18:50.322
It is, isn't it?

1352
01:18:50.357 --> 01:18:51.690
Biggest impact would be here.

1353
01:18:51.725 --> 01:18:53.458
In the Gulf Stream.
Yeah.

1354
01:18:53.494 --> 01:18:55.460
This current here, see it?

1355
01:18:55.496 --> 01:18:57.830
The dumping of ice
off melting Greenland,

1356
01:18:57.865 --> 01:19:01.400
would stop this conveyor belt,
and the Gulf Stream would slow

1357
01:19:01.435 --> 01:19:05.137
down, stopping the transport
of heat from here, to there.

1358
01:19:05.172 --> 01:19:07.639
And then Europe
would get cold toes.

1359
01:19:07.675 --> 01:19:10.642
Because there's a lot of heat
transport from the Tropics,

1360
01:19:10.678 --> 01:19:13.412
across the North Atlantic,
that keeps Europe warm. I mean.

1361
01:19:13.447 --> 01:19:14.713
So Europe would get colder?

1362
01:19:14.748 --> 01:19:16.281
Yeah.

1363
01:19:16.317 --> 01:19:17.416
Cause that's the
big misconception about

1364
01:19:17.451 --> 01:19:19.384
climate change, is that
everything gets warmer.

1365
01:19:19.420 --> 01:19:21.286
Yeah.
Wow.

1366
01:19:21.322 --> 01:19:23.655
And here's the most
advanced precipitation satellite

1367
01:19:23.691 --> 01:19:25.424
in the world.

1368
01:19:25.459 --> 01:19:27.726
This is very important, cause we
think the biggest impact from

1369
01:19:27.761 --> 01:19:31.230
climate change is the moving of
the precipitation belts.

1370
01:19:31.265 --> 01:19:33.632
From the equator
they'll go further out,

1371
01:19:33.667 --> 01:19:37.135
so we're already seeing
signs of a system drought.

1372
01:19:37.171 --> 01:19:38.337
So that causes more
drought in places

1373
01:19:38.372 --> 01:19:40.772
that are already too hot.
Yes.

1374
01:19:40.808 --> 01:19:43.275
And there's a lot of papers
written in the State Department

1375
01:19:43.310 --> 01:19:45.644
and elsewhere, how that
sustained drought has helped

1376
01:19:45.679 --> 01:19:49.681
fuel the conflict of the Syrian
civil war, Darfur, Sudan,

1377
01:19:49.717 --> 01:19:52.651
all these places that are
short of water, short of food.

1378
01:19:52.686 --> 01:19:55.687
Is this throughout the
entire planet or is it just this

1379
01:19:55.723 --> 01:19:57.189
particular region right here?
Nope.

1380
01:19:57.224 --> 01:19:59.057
We expect the whole world.

1381
01:19:59.093 --> 01:20:03.528
We expect bits of India we
expect in the U.S., Oklahoma.

1382
01:20:03.564 --> 01:20:06.131
You know the dust bowl region,
we expect that to get

1383
01:20:06.166 --> 01:20:09.401
much, much drier over the
next few decades.

1384
01:20:09.436 --> 01:20:13.138
Oh my God, and
what about my home state

1385
01:20:13.173 --> 01:20:14.473
of California here?

1386
01:20:14.508 --> 01:20:17.142
Um, not looking
great, I'm afraid.

1387
01:20:17.177 --> 01:20:21.313
Now predicted persistent drought
in the dust bowl, and here,

1388
01:20:21.348 --> 01:20:23.515
for fifty years from now.

1389
01:20:23.550 --> 01:20:26.785
But we're just seeing the
worst drought in 900 years

1390
01:20:26.820 --> 01:20:28.186
here right now.

1391
01:20:28.222 --> 01:20:29.288
So it's coming a bit
earlier than we thought.

1392
01:20:29.323 --> 01:20:31.490
We're talking about this
happening over a period

1393
01:20:31.525 --> 01:20:33.125
of a few decades.

1394
01:20:33.160 --> 01:20:35.260
It's just consistent
not great news.

1395
01:20:35.296 --> 01:20:36.728
No.

1396
01:20:36.764 --> 01:20:39.631
But a lot of people now kinda
confused about the issue.

1397
01:20:39.667 --> 01:20:41.500
You know, the facts
are crystal clear.

1398
01:20:41.535 --> 01:20:44.469
The ice is melting,
the earth is warming,

1399
01:20:44.505 --> 01:20:45.871
the sea level is rising.

1400
01:20:45.906 --> 01:20:47.572
Those are facts.

1401
01:20:47.608 --> 01:20:50.309
Rather than feeling, oh my
God it's hopeless, say, okay,

1402
01:20:50.344 --> 01:20:51.576
this is the problem.

1403
01:20:51.612 --> 01:20:52.844
Let's be realistic.

1404
01:20:52.880 --> 01:20:55.113
Let's find a way out of it.

1405
01:20:55.149 --> 01:20:56.782
And there are ways out of it.

1406
01:20:56.817 --> 01:21:00.619
You know, if we stopped
burning fossil fuel right now,

1407
01:21:00.654 --> 01:21:02.587
the planet would still keep
warming for a little while

1408
01:21:02.623 --> 01:21:04.856
before cooling off again.

1409
01:21:04.892 --> 01:21:08.560
So you're saying
that if we do the right thing,

1410
01:21:08.595 --> 01:21:10.662
we're gonna heat
up, or we're gonna.

1411
01:21:10.698 --> 01:21:13.699
it'll turn off,
then it'll start cooling again.

1412
01:21:13.734 --> 01:21:16.435
Would that Arctic ice
sheet start to then increase

1413
01:21:16.470 --> 01:21:17.602
again?

1414
01:21:17.638 --> 01:21:20.138
Once the cooling started, yeah.

1415
01:21:20.174 --> 01:21:23.241
So there really is
a possibility to repair

1416
01:21:23.277 --> 01:21:25.077
this trajectory that we're on?
Absolutely.

1417
01:21:25.112 --> 01:21:28.080
Interesting.
Yeah. So there's hope.

1418
01:21:28.115 --> 01:21:30.682
You seem to have an
incredibly positive attitude,

1419
01:21:30.718 --> 01:21:33.085
just about everything though.
It's amazing.

1420
01:21:33.120 --> 01:21:36.254
Yeah, I, I do, I'm actually
basically an optimistic

1421
01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:37.356
kind of person.

1422
01:21:37.391 --> 01:21:39.191
I have faith in people.

1423
01:21:39.226 --> 01:21:41.193
I, I really do have
faith in people.

1424
01:21:41.228 --> 01:21:44.663
And I think that once people
come out of the fog of confusion

1425
01:21:44.698 --> 01:21:46.865
or an issue, or initial
uncertainty on an issue,

1426
01:21:46.900 --> 01:21:51.570
and realistically appreciate
it at some level, the threat,

1427
01:21:51.605 --> 01:21:55.774
and they're informed of what the
best action is to deal with it,

1428
01:21:55.809 --> 01:21:57.609
they got on and did it.

1429
01:21:57.644 --> 01:22:00.379
And what seemed like almost
impossible to deal with,

1430
01:22:00.414 --> 01:22:01.780
you know, became possible.

1431
01:22:14.194 --> 01:22:16.328
I still think a lot
about that picture that used

1432
01:22:16.363 --> 01:22:19.431
to hang over above my crib.

1433
01:22:19.466 --> 01:22:22.601
The story of The Garden of
Earthly Delights actually begins

1434
01:22:22.636 --> 01:22:24.736
on the outside of
the painting,

1435
01:22:24.772 --> 01:22:28.440
where. Bosch painted a view
of our Earth on the third day

1436
01:22:28.475 --> 01:22:30.542
of creation.

1437
01:22:30.577 --> 01:22:33.278
It's almost as if he wanted to
show the fragility of our

1438
01:22:33.313 --> 01:22:37.749
planet by depicting the earth
and its atmosphere enclosed

1439
01:22:37.785 --> 01:22:38.850
in glass.

1440
01:22:56.203 --> 01:22:57.769
Pope Francis has
officially released

1441
01:22:57.805 --> 01:23:00.272
his encyclical on the
environment.

1442
01:23:00.307 --> 01:23:03.341
The document is both a call
for immediate action to stop

1443
01:23:03.377 --> 01:23:06.311
global warming, and a
cry for justice for the poor.

1444
01:23:09.416 --> 01:23:14.386
Our common home has fallen
into serious disrepair.

1445
01:23:14.421 --> 01:23:18.790
Hope would have us recognize
that there is always a way out.

1446
01:23:18.826 --> 01:23:22.427
That we can always
redirect our steps,

1447
01:23:22.463 --> 01:23:28.200
that we can always do something
to solve our problems.

1448
01:23:28.235 --> 01:23:32.304
Still, we can see signs that
things are now reaching

1449
01:23:32.339 --> 01:23:34.206
a breaking point.

1450
01:23:37.778 --> 01:23:42.214
This is a direct message from
the pope, it's a huge deal.

1451
01:23:47.187 --> 01:23:49.087
One of the most important
spiritual leader's

1452
01:23:49.123 --> 01:23:50.856
on the planet.

1453
01:23:50.891 --> 01:23:52.190
DiCaprio.

1454
01:23:52.226 --> 01:23:55.327
He has now called upon
the world community to accept

1455
01:23:55.362 --> 01:23:59.431
the modern science
of climate change.

1456
01:23:59.466 --> 01:24:02.100
A pope has never done anything
like this in history.

1457
01:24:16.984 --> 01:24:20.218
Being able to spend time
and sit with the pope

1458
01:24:20.254 --> 01:24:23.188
was a pretty
profound experience.

1459
01:24:24.458 --> 01:24:30.162
This is a book,
Hieronymus Bosch's.

1460
01:24:33.534 --> 01:24:36.168
Uh, it was hanging above
my crib, as a young boy.

1461
01:24:39.273 --> 01:24:40.372
Thank you.

1462
01:24:43.810 --> 01:24:47.212
There was definitely an
urgency in his voice.

1463
01:24:47.247 --> 01:24:52.751
He said that as far as the Paris
conference is concerned, he,

1464
01:24:52.786 --> 01:24:54.753
he felt was a step in
the right direction,

1465
01:24:54.788 --> 01:24:57.389
but certainly not enough.

1466
01:24:57.424 --> 01:25:00.292
He feels we all need to keep
speaking out about this issue

1467
01:25:00.327 --> 01:25:04.829
as loud as we can, and that we
must immediately take action.

1468
01:25:07.000 --> 01:25:11.002
But more than anything, he said
to pray for the human race.

1469
01:25:22.015 --> 01:25:24.883
After everything I've seen,
it's become pretty obvious

1470
01:25:24.918 --> 01:25:26.785
that we're no longer
living in that first,

1471
01:25:26.820 --> 01:25:29.921
unspoiled depiction of Eden.

1472
01:25:29.957 --> 01:25:32.724
We're in that second panel.

1473
01:25:32.759 --> 01:25:36.461
What Bosch called, Human
Kind Before the Flood.

1474
01:25:46.807 --> 01:25:51.409
And what haunts me the
most is that last panel.

1475
01:25:51.445 --> 01:25:54.846
The one with the charred,
blackened skies.

1476
01:25:54.881 --> 01:26:00.218
A planet that we collectively
have left to ruin.

1477
01:26:00.254 --> 01:26:05.357
The question is, can we
change our course in time?

1478
01:26:10.130 --> 01:26:13.765
Now if this was a movie we could
write the ending of this script,

1479
01:26:13.800 --> 01:26:18.403
and we could figure a
way out of this mess.

1480
01:26:18.438 --> 01:26:21.906
But real life doesn't
work like that,

1481
01:26:21.942 --> 01:26:26.444
and we can't pretend that we
know how this is gonna end.

1482
01:26:26.480 --> 01:26:31.983
The only thing that we can do
is control what we do next,

1483
01:26:32.019 --> 01:26:40.091
how we live our lives, what we
consume, how we get involved,

1484
01:26:40.127 --> 01:26:45.096
and how we use our vote to
tell our leaders that we know

1485
01:26:45.132 --> 01:26:49.301
the truth about
climate change.

1486
01:26:50.804 --> 01:26:53.972
The last speaker for
this signing ceremony is

1487
01:26:54.007 --> 01:26:56.274
the Academy Award Best Actor,

1488
01:26:56.310 --> 01:27:01.179
and the United Nations Messenger
of Peace, Mr. Leonardo DiCaprio.

1489
01:27:07.487 --> 01:27:09.387
Thank you Mr.Secretary General for

1490
01:27:09.423 --> 01:27:12.924
the honor to address this body,
and thanks to the distinguished

1491
01:27:12.959 --> 01:27:15.894
climate leaders assembled
here today who are ready

1492
01:27:15.929 --> 01:27:18.363
to take action.

1493
01:27:18.398 --> 01:27:22.167
As a U.N. Messenger of Peace I
have traveled all over the world

1494
01:27:22.202 --> 01:27:26.271
for the last two years, I have
seen cities like Beijing choked

1495
01:27:26.306 --> 01:27:30.408
by industrial pollution, ancient
boreal forests in Canada

1496
01:27:30.444 --> 01:27:33.311
that have been clear cut, and
rainforests in Indonesia

1497
01:27:33.347 --> 01:27:35.146
that have been incinerated.

1498
01:27:35.182 --> 01:27:37.449
In India I met farmers whose
crops have been literally

1499
01:27:37.484 --> 01:27:39.284
washed away.

1500
01:27:39.319 --> 01:27:41.453
In America I've witnessed sea
level rise flooding the streets

1501
01:27:41.488 --> 01:27:43.154
of Miami.

1502
01:27:43.190 --> 01:27:46.191
In Greenland and in the Arctic
I was astonished to see

1503
01:27:46.226 --> 01:27:49.294
that ancient glaciers are
rapidly disappearing,

1504
01:27:49.329 --> 01:27:52.063
well ahead of
scientific predictions.

1505
01:27:52.099 --> 01:27:56.067
All that I have seen and learned
on my journey has absolutely

1506
01:27:56.103 --> 01:27:57.836
terrified me.

1507
01:27:57.871 --> 01:28:00.238
Now think about the shame that
each of us will carry when our

1508
01:28:00.273 --> 01:28:03.375
children and grandchildren look
back and realize that we had

1509
01:28:03.410 --> 01:28:06.845
the means of stopping this
devastation but simply lacked

1510
01:28:06.880 --> 01:28:09.414
the political will to do so.

1511
01:28:09.449 --> 01:28:12.984
Yes, we have achieved
the Paris Agreement.

1512
01:28:13.019 --> 01:28:15.153
More countries have come
together here to sign

1513
01:28:15.188 --> 01:28:18.757
this agreement today than for
any other cause in the history

1514
01:28:18.792 --> 01:28:22.460
of humankind, and that
is reason for hope.

1515
01:28:22.496 --> 01:28:25.263
But unfortunately the evidence
shows us that it will not

1516
01:28:25.298 --> 01:28:26.765
be enough.

1517
01:28:26.800 --> 01:28:29.901
A massive change is
required right now.

1518
01:28:29.936 --> 01:28:33.071
One that leads to a new
collective consciousness.

1519
01:28:33.106 --> 01:28:36.174
A new collective evolution
of the human race,

1520
01:28:36.209 --> 01:28:40.412
inspired and enabled by a sense
of urgency from all of you.

1521
01:28:40.447 --> 01:28:43.214
We can congratulate
each other today,

1522
01:28:43.250 --> 01:28:45.483
but it will mean absolutely
nothing if you return

1523
01:28:45.519 --> 01:28:49.254
to your countries and fail
to push beyond the promises

1524
01:28:49.289 --> 01:28:51.423
of this historic agreement.

1525
01:28:51.458 --> 01:28:54.459
After 21 years of
debates and conferences,

1526
01:28:54.494 --> 01:28:58.463
it is time to declare no
more talk, no more excuses,

1527
01:28:58.498 --> 01:29:02.100
no more ten-year studies, no
more allowing the fossil fuel

1528
01:29:02.135 --> 01:29:05.870
companies to manipulate and
dictate the science and policies

1529
01:29:05.906 --> 01:29:07.839
that affect our future.

1530
01:29:07.874 --> 01:29:10.241
The world is now watching.

1531
01:29:10.277 --> 01:29:13.411
You'll either be lauded
by future generations,

1532
01:29:13.447 --> 01:29:15.180
or vilified by them.

1533
01:29:15.215 --> 01:29:19.217
You are the last
best hope of Earth.

1534
01:29:19.252 --> 01:29:21.319
We ask you to protect it,

1535
01:29:21.354 --> 01:29:26.124
or we, and all living things
we cherish, are history.

